Note to Users of Platinum, v1.96
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If presently using a copy of my 1.95 version of Platinum, you can update to
the 1.96 version simply by copying all the COMMAND files(those files sitting
in the root "Platinum/" directory over those you are presently using). No
changes were made to the formats of the config files, so you needn't have to
re-run the included install script, however you SHOULD run the included
ARexx "Upgrade195" script, which will simply change the version numbers of
your config files to 1.96, so that they can be used with the newer command
files.

Steps On Installing
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Follow these steps for "quick" installtion:

1. Copy the entire "Platinum/" directory to a place on your system you deem
   appropriate for such a file.

   Copy the included libraries to your LIBS: directory if you don't have
   them already(then reboot your system, so they'll be recognized).

2. Inside the included "Platinum/" directory is a file "PL_INSTALL". This
   should be the FIRST file you use. It's written in CNetARexx, and should
   be used from WITHIN CNet Proper, so you'll need to either add it to one
   of your lists, or else use a "RUN ARexx" command to execute it. (Note
   that this file must ALSO be run LOCALLY, as it relies on REQUESTORS for
   some of it's operations). Don't worry about the possibility of this file
   be running remotely, though, as it will make SURE you are LOCAL before it
   continues.

   NOTE: If, for some reason, the install script halts prematurely, I have
         included copies of the config files inside the "Platinum/Configs/"
         directory. You can delete the partial copies created by the install
         scrip